WEBVTT

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:07.649
A formula that uses an aggregate function, such as SUM or COUNT, is

00:00:07.649 --> 00:00:09.902
worked out once for each group.

00:00:09.902 --> 00:00:12.703
This report counts calls for each queue.

00:00:13.933 --> 00:00:17.827
The answer rate adds one for each call that has an answer time,

00:00:17.827 --> 00:00:20.141
and divides by the number of calls.

00:00:20.141 --> 00:00:24.769
Inside such a formula, every field must be inside an aggregate function, and

00:00:24.769 --> 00:00:26.913
Check tells you when one is not.

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:31.662
Apply it, drag it onto Columns, and give it the format P zero,

00:00:31.662 --> 00:00:33.809
so it shows as a percentage.

00:00:33.809 --> 00:00:35.957
Each queue now has its rate.

